    A write that fails because the peer closed or reset the connection leaves the socket open, over TLS as for a
    plain socket (issue #5630): the data the peer sent before it closed is still read, and the read after it returns
    the end of the connection at once - EOF or the reset - and never waits.  The TLS write error carries the errno as
    its argument, like a plain socket's SOCKET-SEND-ERROR.
*/

%modern

%requires QUnit

%exec-class TlsWriteAfterPeerResetTest

